    812:| S202 commit-thread step 5/5 WRAP (Connes amortisation) — synthesise S193–S196 into one statement: do any of {per-query unsmoothed, amortised, CCM-spectral, in-distribution, log-Gaussian-smoothed} regimes break the K = Θ̃(x) per-query floor for π(x) ± 1? | SYNTHESIS+CLOSURE | E | Thread 2 commit step 5/5 WRAP (final synthesis; no new code/experiment). **Unified conditional theorem (Connes-Galway equivalence)**: under the Montgomery pair-correlation random-phase heuristic, for π_{K,h}(x) := R(x) − 2 Σ_{j≤K} Re R(x^{ρ_j}) · exp(−h²γ_j²/2) and any p ∈ (0, 1), the smallest K with Pr(|π(x) − π_{K,h}(x)| ≤ 1/2) ≥ p satisfies K*(x, p, h) = Θ̃(x). Specifically K*(x, 0.5, 0) ≈ 0.0903·x and K*(x, 0.99, 0) ≈ 1.35·x; increasing h ≥ 0 cannot reduce K* (Var_TAIL is h-independent by S196 disjoint-j variance-additivity). Setup-cost asymmetry: CCM dense eigensolver O(K³) vs Hiary 2011 O(K^{17/13}) per-zero locator; ratio K^{22/13} for any Q queries; per-query identical at O(K). **Five regimes simultaneously closed**: (1) per-query unsmoothed (S193 + S195); (2) amortised setup over Q queries (S193); (3) CCM spectral-triple eigenproblem amortised (S193); (4) in-distribution rather than worst-case rounding (S195 with constants 0.0903, 1.35); (5) log-Gaussian-smoothed explicit formula at any bandwidth h ≥ 0 (S196). No regime breaks the floor. **Empirical scope**: 600 unsmoothed (x, K, |err|) triples from S194 + S195 over x ∈ [10^5, 10^7] plus 440 smoothed (x, K, h, |err|) triples from S196 at x ~ 1.78·10^5 across 11 bandwidths. **Closure conditional on the iid-uniform-phase model**; the 26% slope-ratio gap from S195 IS the GUE-vs-Poisson reduction. **Open falsifiers (acknowledged but not needed for Thread 2 closure)**: (a) non-Gaussian smoothing kernels (sinc, sech², Bartlett); (b) empirical extension to x ≥ 10^9; (c) rigorous GUE pair-correlation reduction of K* below x · log^{-c}(x); (d) cross-x amortisation as a different computational model. None known to fail. **Recommended next thread**: all three threads (S82, Connes, Galway) now CLOSED → frontier_gen mode (auto-fire conditions met) OR direct A-grade attempt on A7 plethysm / D44 BC endomotive (S192/S163 flagged). Cites E3.1, E1.5, E2.1, S53 row 706, S193 row 810, S194 row 818, S195 row 816, S196 row 814, Galway 2004, Hiary 2011, Montgomery 1973, Odlyzko 1989. Cross-domain composition: asymmetric setup-cost analysis (S193) + hit-rate-at-fixed-polylog measurement (S194) + GUE random-phase variance estimator with li-asymptotic + Gaussian CLT (S195) + Mellin-domain log-Gaussian kernel (S196), all unified under one conditional theorem. See `archive/sessions/session202_commit_connes_amortisation.md`. | 202 |
    826:| §D48 ATTACK_VECTORS — Bost-Connes endomotive Galois orbits of χ_P-projected KMS_∞ ground states (CCM 2007 *Adv. Math.* 214, 761 = arXiv:math/0512138 §6.2): does the abelian Hilbert-12 Galois action on χ_P-projected pure ground states of the truncated BC algebra carry detectable prime-distribution content beyond Dirichlet equidistribution? (cross-domain: Bost-Connes 1995 *Selecta Math.* 1, 411; CCM 2007 endomotive formalism; Connes-Marcolli 2008 textbook; Marcolli 2005 *Arithmetic Noncommutative Geometry*) | FAIL | E | S203 wild-swing single-session attack on the S163-flagged "highest-A-prior open vector". Closes at mode E (matched-density null) across 14 moduli `N ∈ {30, 60, 90, 105, 120, 210, 330, 420, 510, 630, 840, 1155, 1260, 2310}`. **Construction**: truncate the BC C*-algebra to its commutative sub `\mathcal{A}_N := \mathbb{C}[(\mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z})^*]`; pure KMS_∞ ground states `\phi_\omega(\delta_a) = \omega(a)` parametrised by characters `\omega \in \widehat{G}`, `G = (\mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z})^*`. Define χ_P-projector `P_\chi := Σ_{p ≤ N \text{ prime}, \gcd(p,N)=1} δ_p`; projected functional on the corner reduces to `ω(P_\chi)² · ω(a)`. Two characters give equal projected functionals iff `ω = ω'` or both `ω(P_\chi) = ω'(P_\chi) = 0`; the **zero set** `Z_\chi := {ω : S_\chi(ω) := Σ_p ω(p) = 0}` defines a single merged eq-class. Cyclotomic Galois `(\mathbb{Z}/M\mathbb{Z})^*` (`M = exp G`) acts via `σ_a · ω = ω^a` — Hilbert-12 action restricted to truncation. **Empirics**: `n_zero(χ)` measured against 50-trial random matched-density null `R ⊂ G` with `|R| = |P_N|`. `|z(n_zero)| ≤ 1.1` at every N. Per-bin orbit-length z-scores (14 N × 4–5 bins ≈ 65 tests): max `|z| = 3.39` at `N=60` length-1 bin (a confirmed finite-size artefact — residues `1, 49 mod 60` lack any prime ≤ 60, smallest are 61 and 109; anomaly disappears at `N=120` once these primes fill in); two single-bin `|z| > 3` deviations expected by chance. **No 5σ deviation, no consistent direction across N**. Distinct from CLOSED line 185 (BC partition function = `ζ(β)`, trace-level closure that loses Galois-orbit data by trace-property): D48 is at the **strictly finer ground-state level recommended by CCM 2007 §6.2 as the strongest Galois-data carrier**, and the closure shows the abelian Hilbert-12 part of the endomotive carries no detectable prime content beyond density-matched Dirichlet equidistribution. Distinct from CLOSED line 706 / E3.1 (CCM spectral-triple operator amortisation): D48 is on the BC algebra structure, not the CCM operator. Distinct from E2.29 (Rédei symbol arithmetic-topology Galois cohomology on triples): D48 is non-commutative operator-algebraic on abelianised BC characters. Adds **EDGE E2.30** as the **14th orthogonal pseudorandomness category** for χ_P (non-commutative-arithmetic at BC ground-state level) after E2.13–E2.29; **first project measurement of a non-commutative-arithmetic invariant on χ_P at the BC ground-state level**. **Cross-domain ingredient**: BC + CCM endomotive — appended to `CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md` §1 as "Bost-Connes endomotive ground-state level" USED-E. **Falsifier**: any `N` with `|z(n_zero)| > 5σ` after multiple-comparison adjustment, OR exhibition of a closed-form description of the χ_P eq-class orbit-length distribution in terms of `π(N)` or class-field-theoretic data not captured by matched-density null, OR a polylog Galois-theoretic primality witness extracted from BC ground-state Galois orbits. None observed. **Successors proposed (S203)**: D49 (BC at finite β, retains type III Hecke factor structure not present at β=∞); D50 (Connes-Marcolli-Ramachandran 2005 imaginary-quadratic class fields, `Cl(K)`-action on χ_P-projected ground states for `K = ℚ(√-d)`, `d ∈ {1, 2, 3, 7, 11, 19, 43, 67, 163}` Heegner — different cross-domain ingredient: complex multiplication instead of abelian Hilbert 12). **Channelled mathematician**: Connes (noncommutative geometry, endomotive). See `experiments/algebraic/bc_endomotive_galois_chi_p/`, `archive/sessions/session203_d48_bc_endomotive_galois.md`. | 203 |
