    824	| S198 re-verify-closure (E1.5 entropy bound, A-graded) — adversarial probe of the "CRT reconstruction cannot win" closure: is the per-step h_2(pi(X)/X) bound conservatively framed in a way that misses a non-incremental algorithmic angle? | REFINEMENT+CLOSURE | I | Re-verify-closure session targeting the ONLY A-graded edge in the project. **Adversarial finding**: closure stands. The framing "linear in k" was loose; the precise statement is "constant in k" — combining k coprime moduli incrementally gives the SAME h_2(pi(X)/X) bits per step as a single modulus, regardless of k. **Empirical contribution**: directly measured the JOINT k-moduli conditional entropy `H(joint(x) | joint(x-1))` at k = 1..6, X ∈ {10^4, 10^5, 10^6}. Two competing hypotheses: (H1) Independence — joint = sum of marginals = k·h_2; (H2) Perfect correlation — joint = h_2 (single shared bit). Result at X = 10^6 (joint state space ≪ pi(X) for k ≤ 4): J/h_2 = 1.0000 to 10^{-4}; (H1) decisively rejected. Slight drop at k = 5, 6 (J/h_2 ≈ 0.96 at k=6, X=10^6) is the same finite-state coverage effect S69 §3 documents for m approaching pi(X) — not (H1) signal. **Mechanism**: trivial extension of E1.5. Since pi(x) mod m_i = (pi(x-1) mod m_i + 1[x prime]) mod m_i holds for all i simultaneously, the joint transition is determined by the SINGLE bit b = 1[x prime]; conditioning on joint state, only b is random; so joint H = h_2(P[x prime]) = h_2(pi(X)/X). **Three candidate "missed angles" checked and ruled out**: (A) conditioning on side info x mod 6 — h_2(2p) doesn't vanish faster than h_2(p), constant factor only; (B) larger-step Δ — for Δ such that Δ·pi/X >> 1, increment uniform mod m, conditional H → log_2(min(m, Δ)), trade-off not shortcut; (C) direct (non-incremental) computation of pi(X) mod m — NOT closed by E1.5, this is the central open question (a polylog subroutine for any single m would propagate to polylog pi(X) via CRT). **Two-closure framing made explicit**: closure (i) "no incremental CRT shortcut" — closed by E1.5/S198, sharpened. Closure (ii) "no polylog pi(X) mod m via direct computation" — NOT what E1.5 closes; CLOSED row 244 is the correct anchor for that. Edge entry E1.5 in EDGES.md updated inline with the joint-k-moduli sharpening and the scope-of-closure clarification. **Closure mode I** (information-theoretic, sharpened from E in row 243). What's NEW: (a) direct empirical measurement of joint k-moduli entropy (S69 measured per-modulus marginals only); (b) sharpened wording "constant in k" replacing "linear in k"; (c) explicit two-closure framing distinguishing incremental from non-incremental. Cites E1.5 (refined), CLOSED rows 243, 244, E1.6 (compatible). Cross-domain ingredient: NONE (within-project information-theoretic verification). **Falsifier**: any (k, X) cell with prod(m_i) << pi(X)/100 yielding J/h_2 ≠ 1.0000 ± 10^{-4}, OR exhibiting a polylog non-incremental subroutine for pi(X) mod m for any single m (would resolve closure (ii) regardless of E1.5). See `experiments/information_theory/joint_kmoduli_entropy/`, `archive/sessions/session198_reverify_e1_5.md`. | 198 |
