## Summary

**Mode:** wild_swing / cross-domain attack on ATTACK_VECTORS §D.D3 (free probability + matrix models).
**Cross-domain ingredient:** Bryc-Dembo-Jiang 2006 universal LSD `γ_T`, `γ_H` for real symmetric Toeplitz/Hankel matrices with i.i.d. entries; Hammond-Miller 2005 good-pair-partition expansion.
**Self-grade: B-grade case (i)** — refinement of E2.21 (Newman L^∞ flatness) from L^∞ point evaluation to L^k integral evaluation via Szegő-Toeplitz spectral moments.

**Result:** χ_P decisively VIOLATES BDJ universality with a clean divergent-scaling law:
- `m_4(χ_P-T, N) ≈ 2.95·N/log²N` (BDJ univ: 8/3) — measured 46.5 → 160.4 across N=500..3500
- `m_4(χ_P-H, N) ≈ 1.66·N/log²N` (BDJ univ: 2) — measured 22.3 → 85.6
- `λ̃_max(χ_P-T) ≈ (4/π)·√(N/log N)` — empirical constant 1.337 → 1.282 monotone descent toward 4/π=1.273
- `λ̃_max(χ_P-H) ≈ 1.06·√(N/log N)`
- top-eigenvalue contributes **89.0% (T) / 76.2% (H) of m_4 universally** across all four N

Hankel m_4 prediction matches measurement to 0.0% rel err at N=2000, ≤3.5% across all N.

**Mechanism:** the q=2 parity major-arc spike of E2.21 — `|F_N(e^{iπ})| ≈ π(N)−2` produces a single rank-1 component with eigenvalue ≈ `(1/√log N)·N`; after BDJ scaling `/√N` gives `√(N/log N)`. By Szegő, m_4 ≈ L^4 norm of the χ_P symbol = additive energy of primes.

**Why B and not A:** mechanism reduces to known E2.21; no algorithmic upside (Lanczos at Ω(N log N)).

**Files modified:** EDGES.md (E2.31 added), CLOSED_PATHS.md (S204 row), ATTACK_VECTORS.md (D3 marked closed + Closed-attacks entry), CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md (BDJ row USED-I), `experiments/constructions/bdj_toeplitz_hankel_chi_p/` (new), `archive/sessions/session204_d3_bdj_toeplitz_hankel.md`, SESSION_INSIGHTS.md S204 entry, `.run_state = 204`.

**Successors flagged:** D3.a (Liouville BDJ test, predicts FULL universality — sharpest mechanism test), D3.b (parity-subtracted χ_P), D3.c (γ_M Markov LSD).
